{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit 1731 took Verified -1 — triaged as INHERITED from main, not a defect in this change. Not rechecked.\n\nSignature: all four pytest cells (macos py3.13, ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13) failed in 25-33s, i.e. at the gate stage before any test ran. Log (run 31730396829) says: 'src/rebar file(s) over the 800-LOC hard cap (split them — there is no allowlist): 808 src/rebar/_config_schema.py'.\n\nMeasured rather than assumed:\n- blob at origin/main for src/rebar/_config_schema.py is 808 lines (git ls-tree origin/main + cat-file blob).\n- the commit before the stale-submit, a147945aae, had it at exactly 800 — sitting on the cap.\n- the commit that pushed it over is d2dea317ec 'Trigger compaction from the close, out of band', the erroneously-submitted change 1727 that ticket e30d-b5e7-f4de-4f91 (zincous-activated-ant) exists to prevent.\n- this change touches five files, none under src/: the portability rubric, docs/plan-review-gate.md, AGENTS.md, and two test modules. It cannot move a src/rebar line count.\n\nSo main is red for every change based on it, deterministically. Per the flaky-vs-environmental rule this batch is landing (9b79-56ba-0d16-4c49), a deterministic gate failure is neither a flake nor an environmental fault, so 'recheck' is the wrong remedy — it would fail identically. Two fix-forwards are racing to land; the plan is to wait for either, rebase 1731 onto the fixed main, and re-push. Not fixing _config_schema.py from this session: three sessions editing one file is how the original incident happened."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786645620787547001,"uuid":"88b02696-1240-4b6b-a75b-56f4a19a3428"}